+## Due times and going back to 1.4.0
+
+Every ticket in the data file has a `due`. At the first start of 1.5.0 the tickets without one get theirs, from their own
+creation time and priority and the hours then set, and the file is rewritten at once; new tickets get theirs when created.
+This happens whether or not `DUE_TIMES` is `on`: switch it on only after the first start has written the file, and until
+then the API answers exactly as 1.4.0 does.
+
+To go back to 1.4.0, stop the service and start 1.4.0 on the same file: the file is still version 1 and 1.4.0 ignores
+`due`, so every ticket shows. 1.4.0 rewrites the file without `due`, so after going forward again the tickets get new due
+times from their creation time at that first start; keep a copy of the file from before 1.4.0 ran if the times matter.
+
 ## Notifications
 
 A change that should tell someone something (a ticket received, a ticket resolved) enqueues a notification in the outbox
